      "body": "The V13 model and checkpoint identities are recovered exactly; the stronger audio corpus still differs from the old joint corpus. This stage on #4815 adds a stateless adapter to real frozen HX/GRU/SSM checkpoints and predeclares CPU engineering replay: original six-prefix parity, actual subprocess pending-read recovery, RESET rejection and a 128-step repeated historical stream. It also freezes a single historical real-media decode/clock diagnostic.\n\nSource is published before numerical execution. Results will be appended with their exact source commit; this source checkpoint does not assert numerical PASS.\n\nThe known-exposure inventory has 288 official-audio TRAIN recordings and 24 joint TRAIN recordings, with zero recording or actor intersection. It is a partial known exposure union, not a complete historical exclusion ledger. Text/image and 1536-dimensional audio are rejected by the actual V13 row55 adapter until proper adapters are trained and qualified.\n\nOriginal parameter counts differ (HX 31,430; GRU 32,550; SSM 29,382), and original training time was not matched. No new training or quality benefit is claimed. Strong common frontend, new independent worlds, continuous first-passage/reset semantics, equal-budget strong comparisons and target GPU/energy qualification remain HOLD.",
